  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "After basic finite-dimensional norm equivalence and scalar compactness are supplied, the original new core constructs canonical graded lifts and controls weakly tame cross terms by a uniform multi-scale coercivity estimate. The fixed lemma then inductively truncates every graded coordinate while simultaneously maintaining nearest-site equality for all points in a compact set and all sufficiently large degeneration parameters. It selects representatives in finitely many graded fibers, balances their tails against excluded sites using separated scales, and closes finite-prefix discreteness; this uniform rank-dependent discrete optimization mechanism is above ordinary qualification compactness.",
